      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2001 S. Karger AG, Basel",
        "AbstractText": "Neuropathic pain is a very difficult problem with which the neurosurgeon frequently must deal. The neurosurgical methods to be considered are: (1) modulative, by using neurostimulation or implanted drug delivery systems, and (2) ablative, by making selective therapeutic lesions in well-defined and identified targets proven to sustain pain mechanisms (especially DREZotomy)."
      },
